## 6. Real-Time Anomaly Detection

### Statistical Anomaly Detection

**Z-Score Method**:
```csharp
public class AnomalyDetector
{
    public bool IsAnomaly(double value, double mean, double stdDev, double threshold = 3.0)
    {
        if (stdDev == 0) return false;
        
        var zScore = Math.Abs((value - mean) / stdDev);
        return zScore > threshold;
    }
    
    public async Task<List<Anomaly>> DetectAnomaliesAsync(List<SensorReading> readings)
    {
        var values = readings.Select(r => r.Value).ToList();
        var mean = values.Average();
        var stdDev = CalculateStandardDeviation(values, mean);
        
        var anomalies = new List<Anomaly>();
        
        foreach (var reading in readings)
        {
            if (IsAnomaly(reading.Value, mean, stdDev))
            {
                anomalies.Add(new Anomaly
                {
                    Reading = reading,
                    ZScore = Math.Abs((reading.Value - mean) / stdDev),
                    DetectedAt = DateTime.UtcNow
                });
            }
        }
        
        return anomalies;
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Real-time detection
- Statistical accuracy
- Configurable thresholds
- Low latency

