## 7. Channel-Based Producer-Consumer

### What are Channels?

**Channels** provide a way to communicate between async producers and consumers.

### MaritimeIQ Implementation

```csharp
private readonly Channel<ConsumeResult<string, string>> _processingChannel;
private readonly ChannelWriter<ConsumeResult<string, string>> _writer;
private readonly ChannelReader<ConsumeResult<string, string>> _reader;

public MaritimeStreamingProcessor()
{
    var options = new BoundedChannelOptions(1000)
    {
        FullMode = BoundedChannelFullMode.Wait
    };
    
    _processingChannel = Channel.CreateBounded<ConsumeResult<string, string>>(options);
    _writer = _processingChannel.Writer;
    _reader = _processingChannel.Reader;
}

// Producer
public async Task ProduceAsync(ConsumeResult<string, string> result)
{
    await _writer.WriteAsync(result);
}

// Consumer
public async Task ConsumeAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    await foreach (var result in _reader.ReadAllAsync(cancellationToken))
    {
        await ProcessEventAsync(result, cancellationToken);
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Decoupled producer/consumer
- Back-pressure handling
- Efficient async processing
- Scalable

